s6-1-p47 = prose (cons "**Substitution acts on reductions.** If \(r:t\longrightarrow u\) is a generating reduction and \(\theta\) is a well-typed substitution, define \(\mathsf{substStep}(\theta,r)\) by induction on the reduction constructor: a beta step is sent to the corresponding substituted beta step, and a congruence step is sent to the congruence of the recursively substituted step. Thus" nil)
